{"question_id":"1l57t743a","chapter":"some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry","chapterGroup":"physical-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"easy","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en","hi"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperId":"jee-main-2022-online-27th-june-morning-shift","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2022 (Online) 27th June Morning Shift","permalink":"ptwo-elements-a-and-b-which-form-015-moles-of-asub2su-jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-kygsod9svlcohsa5","question":{"en":{"direction":null,"content":"<p>Two elements A and B which form 0.15 moles of A<sub>2</sub>B and AB<sub>3</sub> type compounds. If both A<sub>2</sub>B and AB<sub>3</sub> weigh equally, then the atomic weight of A is _____________ times of atomic weight of B.</p>","options":[],"correct_options":[],"answer":"2","explanation":"<p>Let atomic weight of A = x</p>\n<p>and atomic weight of B = y</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.509ex\" height=\"1.251ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -471 667 553\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2234\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2234\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> Molar mass of A<sub>2</sub>B = 2x + y</p>\n<p>and molar mass of AB<sub>3</sub> = x + 3y</p>\n<p>Now, weight of 0.15 moles of A<sub>2</sub>B = (2x + y) 0.15</p>\n<p>and weight of 0.15 moles of AB<sub>3</sub> = (x + 3y) 0.15</p>\n<p>Given, weight of 0.15 moles of A<sub>2</sub>B and AB<sub>3</sub> are equal.</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.509ex\" height=\"1.251ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -471 667 553\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://