ht=\"1.545ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 708 683\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"42\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-42\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> \u0915\u0940 \u092a\u0930\u092e\u093e\u0923\u094d\u0935\u093f\u0915 \u0938\u0902\u0939\u0924\u093f \u0915\u0940 _______________ \u0917\u0941\u0928\u093e \u0939\u094b\u0917\u0940\u0964</p>","options":[],"correct_options":[],"answer":"2","explanation":null}},"section":["chapter","paper"],"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":120000,"topic":"mole-concept","type":"integer","year":2022,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":[],"bookmark":{"en":{"title":"JEE Main 2022 (Online) 27th June Morning Shift","subTitle":"Some Basic Concepts of Chemistry \u2022 Chemistry","excerpt":"Two elements A and B which form 0.15 moles of A2B and AB3 type compounds. If both A2B and AB3 weigh equally, then the atomic weight of A is _____________ times of atomic weight of B."},"hi":{"title":"JEE Main 2022 (Online) 27th June Morning Shift","subTitle":"Some Basic Concepts of Chemistry \u2022 Chemistry","excerpt":"\u0926\u094b \u0924\u0924\u094d\u0935 $$\\mathrm{A}$$ \u0924\u0925\u093e $$\\mathrm{B}, \\mathrm{A}_{2} \\mathrm{B}$$ \u0924\u0925\u093e $$\\mathrm{AB}_{3}$$ \u092a\u094d\u0930\u0915\u093e\u0930 \u0915\u0947 $$0.15 ~\\mathrm{moles}$$ \u092f\u094c\u0917\u093f\u0915 \u092c\u0928\u093e\u0924\u0947 \u0939\u0948\u0902\u0964 \u092f\u0926\u093f $$\\mathrm{A}_{2} \\mathrm{B}$$ \u0924\u0925\u093e $$\\mathrm{AB}_{3}$$ \u0915\u0940 \u0938\u0902\u0939\u0924\u093f \u0938\u092e\u093e\u0928 \u0939\u094b \u0924\u094b $$\\mathrm{A}$$ \u0915\u0940..."}},"yearKey":"jee-main-2022-online-27th-june-morning-shift","qKey":"ptwo-elements-a-and-b-which-form-015-moles-of-asub2su-jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-kygsod9svlcohsa5","content":"<p>Two elements A and B which form 0.15 moles of A<sub>2</sub>B and AB<sub>3</sub> type compounds. If both A<sub>2</sub>B and AB<sub>3</sub> weigh equally, then the atomic weight of A is _____________ times of atomic weight of B.</p>","explanation":"<p>Let atomic weight of A = x</p>\n<p>and atomic weight of B = y</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.509ex\" height=\"1.251ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -471 667 553\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2234\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2234\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> Molar mass of A<sub>2</sub>B = 2x + y</p>\n<p>and molar mass of AB<sub>3</sub> = x + 3y</p>\n<p>Now, weight of 0.15 moles of A<sub>2</sub>B = (2x + y) 0.15</p>\n<p>and weight of 0.15 moles of AB<sub>3</sub> = (x + 3y) 0.15</p>\n<p>Given, weight of 0.15 moles of A<sub>2</sub>B and AB<sub>3</sub> are equal.</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.509ex\" height=\"1.251ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -471 667 553\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2234\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2234\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> (2x + y)0.15 = (x + 3y)0.15</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.054ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.242ex\" role=\"img\" focus